<main class="dashboard">


<div class="dashboard-header">

<h1>
🔢 Mathematics Formula Library
</h1>

<p>
Quick reference formulas for mathematics teaching and lessons.
</p>

</div>


<div class="dashboard-grid">


<div class="dashboard-card">

<h2>
📐 Geometry
</h2>

<p>
Area, perimeter and circumference formulas.
</p>

<hr>

<p>
<strong>Rectangle Area</strong><br>
A = l × w
</p>

<p>
<strong>Rectangle Perimeter</strong><br>
P = 2(l + w)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Triangle Area</strong><br>
A = ½bh
</p>

<p>
<strong>Circle Area</strong><br>
A = πr²
</p>

<p>
<strong>Circle Circumference</strong><br>
C = 2πr
</p>

</div>


<div class="dashboard-card">

<h2>
📦 Mensuration
</h2>

<p>
Surface area and volume formulas.
</p>

<hr>

<p>
<strong>Rectangular Prism Volume</strong><br>
V = lwh
</p>

<p>
<strong>Cylinder Volume</strong><br>
V = πr²h
</p>

<p>
<strong>Cylinder Surface Area</strong><br>
SA = 2πr² + 2πrh
</p>

<p>
<strong>Sphere Volume</strong><br>
V = ⁴⁄₃πr³
</p>

<p>
<strong>Sphere Surface Area</strong><br>
SA = 4πr²
</p>

</div>


<div class="dashboard-card">

<h2>
🔢 Algebra
</h2>

<p>
Common algebraic identities and equations.
</p>

<hr>

<p>
<strong>Linear Equation</strong><br>
y = mx + c
</p>

<p>
<strong>Difference of Squares</strong><br>
a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Perfect Square</strong><br>
(a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b²
</p>

<p>
<strong>Perfect Square</strong><br>
(a − b)² = a² − 2ab + b²
</p>

<p>
<strong>Quadratic Formula</strong><br>
x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / 2a
</p>

</div>


<div class="dashboard-card">

<h2>
📈 Coordinate Geometry
</h2>

<p>
Formulas for lines, gradients and points.
</p>

<hr>

<p>
<strong>Gradient</strong><br>
m = (y₂ − y₁) / (x₂ − x₁)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Distance</strong><br>
d = √((x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Midpoint</strong><br>
M = ((x₁ + x₂)/2, (y₁ + y₂)/2)
</p>

</div>


<div class="dashboard-card">

<h2>
📊 Statistics
</h2>

<p>
Common statistical measures.
</p>

<hr>

<p>
<strong>Mean</strong><br>
Mean = Sum of values / Number of values
</p>

<p>
<strong>Range</strong><br>
Range = Maximum − Minimum
</p>

<p>
<strong>Probability</strong><br>
P(E) = Favourable outcomes / Total outcomes
</p>

</div>


<div class="dashboard-card">

<h2>
📐 Trigonometry
</h2>

<p>
Right-triangle trigonometric relationships.
</p>

<hr>

<p>
<strong>Sine</strong><br>
sin θ = Opposite / Hypotenuse
</p>

<p>
<strong>Cosine</strong><br>
cos θ = Adjacent / Hypotenuse
</p>

<p>
<strong>Tangent</strong><br>
tan θ = Opposite / Adjacent
</p>

<p>
<strong>Pythagoras</strong><br>
a² + b² = c²
</p>

</div>


